## Reliability and caching

- Fetch series independently and expose per-source health.
- Cache successful server responses for roughly one hour and coalesce duplicate in-flight requests.
- Allow manual refresh to bypass normal response caching.
- Retain successful observations in browser local storage.
- If a request fails, keep any saved observations visible and clearly mark them as an offline snapshot.
- If no observations exist, show Unavailable and a useful retry action.
- Apply request timeouts and validate upstream response shapes.
- Do not require a database.
- Do not add background scheduling or automatic refresh while the application is closed.

